
# --- Discord bot (npm run bot) ---
DISCORD_TOKEN=
# Free project id from https://cloud.walletconnect.com. The bot reads this name directly; the website build needs the same value again under
# VITE_WALLETCONNECT_PROJECT_ID (Vite only exposes VITE_-prefixed vars to client code) — add qmax.exchange (or your domain) as an allowed origin
# for the project at cloud.walletconnect.com, or wallets may show the connection as unverified.
WALLETCONNECT_PROJECT_ID=
VITE_WALLETCONNECT_PROJECT_ID=
# The subscription's price in dollars a month (trading and arbitrage). Converted to QU at the live price when someone subscribes.
BOT_SUBSCRIPTION_USD=1
# Testing only: a fixed QU price instead of dollars (the live price is then not used)
BOT_SUBSCRIPTION_PRICE_QU=100000
# Optional: where phones can reach the API (it serves the /open page that opens the wallet app), e.g. https://api.example.com
# BOT_PUBLIC_URL=
# Optional: DISCORD_GUILD_ID=<your test server's id> makes commands appear instantly there
# Optional: BOT_FREE_UNTIL=2026-11-06  makes trading and the arbitrage details free for everyone on Discord until then (a launch period; no payment, no receipt)
# BOT_ALERTS_PRICE_QU=100000  sells the bot's alerts on their own: the bot checks the market for every alert about every minute, which uses real resources. With it set, /subscribe buys
#   alerts for BOT_SUB_DAYS days at this price (through QPayhub) and an alert of any kind needs it; trading, quotes, charts and the rest stay free. Unset: alerts are free.
# Support QMax goes through a Q+Pay tip jar: create one in the QPay dashboard (useqpay.com) and paste its link here (https only). The website's Support
# dialog and the bot's /support then show a "Tip with Q+Pay" button and a QR of it. Unset, they show the QMax address (SUPPORT_ADDRESS, default the address QMax is paid to).
# SUPPORT_URL=https://useqpay.com/tipjar/<id>
# Optional: BOT_SUB_DAYS=30  BOT_SLIPPAGE_BPS=100  QMAX_API_URL=http://localhost:8787  BOT_DATA_DIR=.cache/bot

# --- Who may use the API ---
# API_ACCESS=free (default): everyone, no key, no billing, limited per IP (API_FREE_PER_MIN, default 60 a minute). Only the Discord bot's subscription is paid.
# API_ACCESS=billing: the old prepaid per-call prices and x402 sessions. API_ACCESS=private: only API_KEY gets in.
# API_MAX_PRICE_QU=100  sells Max plans (GET /v1/max) to agents in free mode: from a prepaid key's balance (POST /v1/keys, GET /v1/topup) or inside an x402 session. 0 or unset: free.
#   The website's own Max and QMax's own keys never pay; every other endpoint stays free.
# The website's pass is off (trading is free). Build it with VITE_REQUIRE_PASS=on to ask for the pass again.
# --- Prepaid API for other sites (only with API_ACCESS=billing) ---
# Your own key (the Discord bot uses it too): never charged or limited. Set the same value for the bot.
API_KEY=
# The owner's key, for the subscriber list, profit sharing, payouts and stats (openssl rand -hex 24). The Discord bot must NOT have it: if it is
# tricked into leaking its API_KEY, that key reads the market and nothing else. Used by npm run payout. Unset: API_KEY opens these endpoints too.
ADMIN_KEY=
# Agents can buy a session by x402 (pay QPayhub, present the receipt): API_SESSION_PRICE_QU=10000 API_SESSION_SECONDS=3600 API_X402=off to disable.
# X402_TICKET_SECRET and X402_GRANT_SECRET sign tickets and sessions; if unset, random ones are made and kept in .cache. PUBLIC_BASE_URL is this API's public address, with any path prefix (https://qmax.exchange/api behind nginx): x402 challenges, the OpenAPI document and /llms.txt tell agents to use it.
# Optional: API_SPLIT_PRICE_QU=100  API_ARBITRAGE_PRICE_QU=50  API_MIN_TOPUP_QU=10000  API_FREE_PER_MIN=60  TRUST_PROXY=1 (behind your own proxy)  API_METER=off
# Price history from before QMax started recording is rebuilt from past trades (QX fills, QSwap swaps) in the archive. TRADE_HISTORY=off to disable; TRADE_HISTORY_DAYS=210 sets how far back (the archive has events from about April 2026).
# Who trades through QMax (read with GET /v1/stats and your API_KEY): the app reports each trade's transaction id, QMax checks it against the archive, and payments to your address are read from QPayhub. TRADE_USAGE=off turns the counting off.
# Subscribers share QMax's fee income (computed from the chain; see README "Subscribers and profit sharing"). PROFIT_SHARE=off turns it off.
# PROFIT_SHARE_PCT=75            share of each month's net income (what QPayhub forwarded to you) that goes into the pool
# PROFIT_SHARE_CAP=1             most a wallet can earn in a month, as a multiple of what it paid (0 = no cap)
# PROFIT_SHARE_START=2026-10     first month that counts (default: the month the server first ran with this on)
# PROFIT_SHARE_MIN_PAYOUT_QU=1000  smaller balances wait for the next payout
# PROFIT_SHARE_EXCLUDE=ID1,ID2   wallets left out entirely (your own test wallets); your QMax address is always left out
# PROFIT_SHARE_INCOME=pass,subscription,api-topup,session   which payments count as income;  PROFIT_SHARE_ELIGIBLE=subscription   whose payers share
# BOT_SUB_DAYS=30 is what the server assumes one subscription lasts, the same value the bot uses.
# The payout itself is signed by you: QMAX_PAYOUT_SEED (the QMax address's seed) is read only by `npm run payout -- --send`, from your own shell.
# Token-to-token swaps have no size limit. To add one, set the most QU a swap plan may put at risk. MCP/agents: see mcp/README.md.
# SWAP_MAX_OUTLAY_QU=100000000

# My assets and History read a wallet's trades from the public archive, which limits how often it is asked. A wallet's ledger is kept in memory and reused for this many seconds by everyone who asks (30 to 3600, default 300). Prices of sales (the worth if sold now) are shared for 30 seconds.
# LEDGER_CACHE_SECONDS=300

# QMax Pro (website build settings; see "Max, and QMax Pro" in the README). Max is free for everyone to try for 14 days from their first use.
# Nothing is charged until a price is set.
# VITE_PRO_MODE=trial          trial (default) | free (always free) | paid (a pass from the first use)
# VITE_PRO_TRIAL_DAYS=14
# VITE_PRO_PRICE_QU=0          what a pass costs in QU; 0 = not charging yet; at least 100 (QPayhub's minimum) once set
# VITE_PRO_DAYS=30             how long a pass lasts
# One pass covers the payer and up to 14 listed addresses; the server decides who is covered from the chain (GET /v1/pro). It reads the same settings
# without the VITE_ prefix if you set them (otherwise the VITE_ ones above), and PRO_COVER=off turns the endpoints off.
# PRO_DAYS=30
# PRO_PRICE_QU=0               a payment under this (and under QPayhub's 100 QU minimum) is not a pass

# Where the welcome window's Subscribe button goes: a Discord invite (or server) link. Set when the website is built. Without it the button explains how to subscribe.
# VITE_DISCORD_URL=https://discord.gg/yourinvite
